ures\n- Minimal GUI (Tkinter)\n- Autosave after a short pause in typing\n- Tags (comma-separated)\n- Quick search by title, tags, and full-text content (unencrypted notes)\n- Optional encryption for note content (titles/tags remain plaintext for search)\n- Local-only storage; no telemetry\n\n## Requirements\n- Python 3.8+\n- Tkinter (generally included with Python; on some Linux distros you may need to install `python3-tk`)\n- Optional: `cryptography` for encryption\n\nInstall optional dependency:\n```\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## Installation and Run\n1. Clone or copy this repository/app files.\n2. (Optional) Create a virtual environment.\n3. Install optional dependencies:\n```\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n4. Run the app:\n```\npython3 quick_notes.py\n```\n\n## Data Storage Location\nBy default, the app stores the SQLite DB in a platform-appropriate location:\n- Linux: `~/.local/share/local-quick-notes/notes.db`\n- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Local Quick Notes/notes.db`\n- Windows: `%APPDATA%/LocalQuickNotes/notes.db`\n\nOverride the location with an environment variable:\n```\nQUICK_NOTES_DB=/path/to/notes.db python3 quick_notes.py\n```\n\n## Encryption\n- Click \"Enable encryption\" to set a passphrase. This encrypts note content using a key derived with PBKDF2 (SHA-256) and Fernet.\n- Only note content is encrypted; titles/tags remain plaintext so you can still search notes.\n- On next launch, you'll be prompted to unlock. You can cancel to use the app without unlocking; encrypted notes will appear as \"[Encrypted]\".\n\n## Search\n- The search box filters notes by title/tags and also performs full-text search across note content for unencrypted notes using SQLite FTS5.\n- Notes saved with encryption cannot be searched by content (only by title and tags).\n\n## Keyboard Shortcuts\n- Ctrl+N: New note\n- Ctrl+F: Focus search\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- If encryption is unavailable, ensure `cryptography` is installed.\n- On Linux, if Tkinter isn't present, install `python3-tk` via your package manager.\n\n## Roadmap (Next)\n- Export/import (e.g., Markdown, encrypted archive)\n- Dark theme toggle\n- Tag filters and reordering\n\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/README.md', path='/workspace/README.md', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/README.md\\n+++ /workspace/README.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+# Local Quick Notes\\n@@ -1,0 +3,65 @@\\n+A minimal, privacy-focused notes scratchpad with autosave, tags, quick search, and optional end-to-end encryption of note content. Data is stored locally in a SQLite database.\\n+\\n+## Features\\n+- Minimal GUI (Tkinter)\\n+- Autosave after a short pause in typing\\n+- Tags (comma-separated)\\n+- Quick search by title, tags, and full-text content (unencrypted notes)\\n+- Optional encryption for note content (titles/tags remain plaintext for search)\\n+- Local-only storage; no telemetry\\n+\\n+## Requirements\\n+- Python 3.8+\\n+- Tkinter (generally included with Python; on some Linux distros you may need to install `python3-tk`)\\n+- Optional: `cryptography` for encryption\\n+\\n+Install optional dependency:\\n+```\\n+pip install -r requirements.txt\\n+```\\n+\\n+## Installation and Run\\n+1. Clone or copy this repository/app files.\\n+2. (Optional) Create a virtual environment.\\n+3. Install optional dependencies:\\n+```\\n+pip install -r requirements.txt\\n+```\\n+4. Run the app:\\n+```\\n+python3 quick_notes.py\\n+```\\n+\\n+## Data Storage Location\\n+By default, the app stores the SQLite DB in a platform-appropriate location:\\n+- Linux: `~/.local/share/local-quick-notes/notes.db`\\n+- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Local Quick Notes/notes.db`\\n+- Windows: `%APPDATA%/LocalQuickNotes/notes.db`\\n+\\n+Override the location with an environment variable:\\n+```\\n+QUICK_NOTES_DB=/path/to/notes.db python3 quick_notes.py\\n+```\\n+\\n+#